{%- comment -%}
  What the search shows before anything is typed (2026-10-21, owner: „don't keep it like theirs, add it“): the
  popular searches on the left and the bestsellers as product cards on the right, so the search is never empty.
  moonmagic.com shows its „Popular searches“ and „Most loved“ only once something is typed.

  Not placed on any page: assets/cj-search.js fetches it (/?section_id=cj-search-start) the first time the search
  opens, so no page carries these cards until someone opens the search. The bestsellers are the homepage row's own
  collection, „all“ (templates/index.json, Най-продавани), its first eight.
{%- endcomment -%}
<div class="cj-search__panel">
  {%- render 'cj-search-popular' -%}

  {%- assign cj_best = collections['all'] -%}
  {%- if cj_best.products_count > 0 -%}
    <div class="cj-search__products">
      <h2 class="cj-search__label">Най-продавани</h2>
      <ul class="cj-search__grid list-unstyled" role="list">
        {%- for product in cj_best.products limit: 8 -%}
          <li class="cj-search__card">
            {% render 'card-product',
              card_product: product,
              media_aspect_ratio: 'square',
              lazy_load: true,
              show_secondary_image: true,
              section_id: section.id,
              product_view_context: 'search'
            %}
          </li>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </ul>
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Search: before typing",
  "settings": []
}
{% endschema %}
